OAO6SJc625YBK","user":{"login":"charjr","id":102669158,"node_id":"U_kgDOBh6bZg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102669158?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr","html_url":"https://github.com/charjr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T08:54:04Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T08:54:51Z","body":"@Lucas-Code27 \n\n> overlaps are just areas and bodies inside the area's collision shape\n\n> overlapping areas are other area nodes in the area's collision shape\n\nIf `overlaps` are _areas and bodies_ inside the collision shape,\nthen `overlapping areas` sounds like it is a subset of `overlaps`\n\nThat is the conclusion I draw from the documentation currently. But when I draw that conclusion, the following question come to mind:\n\nHow could the superset `overlaps` be calculated before its subsets?\nThe docs state `overlaps` are calculated before the physics step, but `overlapping_areas` and `overlapping_bodies` are calculated afterwards, during the physics step\n\nAgain, I may be misunderstanding, but I cannot find a description for these properties. This is why I feel something is amiss, either an inconsistency, or a missing detail.\n\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068493898/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068528008","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108585#issuecomment-3068528008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108585","id":3068528008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc625gWI","user":{"login":"charjr","id":102669158,"node_id":"U_kgDOBh6bZg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102669158?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr","html_url":"https://github.com/charjr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T09:01:37Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T09:01:37Z","body":"@Rindbee \n> You need to understand the descriptions in the document in conjunction with the names of methods, properties, parameters, etc. You may want to add an implicit `self` if necessary.\n\nI apologize, but I don't quite understand what you mean by adding an implicit `self` in this context.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068528008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_v