ues/comments/3068636319","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108585#issuecomment-3068636319","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108585","id":3068636319,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6256yf","user":{"login":"charjr","id":102669158,"node_id":"U_kgDOBh6bZg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102669158?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr","html_url":"https://github.com/charjr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T09:34:49Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T09:34:49Z","body":"> `self.has_overlapping_areas()` means: whether (the return value type is `bool` type) it(self) has overlapping area.\n> \n> `self.overlaps_area(area)` means: whether it(self) overlaps the `area`.\n\nAh I see what you were referring to, those methods I do understand.\n\nIn my case, I was scouring the Area3D class reference, trying to work out for certain when overlapping bodies are actually calculated and the best time to get them. \n\n1. Because the _list of overlaps_ is never explicitly defined, I have to start making assumptions.\n2. I assume that the _list of overlaps_ is a superset of _overlapping areas_ and _overlapping bodies_.\n3. I get confused because _overlaps_ is, somehow, updated before its subsets.\n\nI've updated my original post to be a bit clearer.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068636319/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068701828","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108585#issuecomment-3068701828","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108585","id":3068701828,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc626KyE","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T09:51:32Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T09:54:26Z","body":">     2. I assume that the _list of overlaps_ is a superset of _overlapping areas_ and _overlapping bodies_.\n\n\nTake a look at the code. They are actually describing the same thing, but because the descriptions were added in different PRs, they are referred to using different words. Of course, it may also be because of the method name.\n\nBut the timing in the descriptions seems inconsistent, which may need to be unified.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068701828/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068838742","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108585#issuecomment-3068838742","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108585","id":3068838742,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc626sNW","user":{"login":"charjr","id":102669158,"node_id":"U_kgDOBh6bZg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102669158?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr","html_url":"https://github.com/charjr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T10:20:37Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T10:37:36Z","body":"> Take a look at the code. They are actually describing the same thing, \n\nYou're right. \n- Both `get_overlapping_areas` and `has_overlapping_areas` access an `area_map`. \n- Both `get_overlapping_bodies` and `has_overlapping_bodies` access a `body_map`.\n\nWhen you said to look at the code, as a programmer by trade, this wasn't a huge hurdle.\nBeginners, however, should be able to rely on the docs, without diving into the implementation.\n\n> but because the descriptions were added in different PRs, they are referred to using different words. Of course, it may also be because of the method name.\n\nI think, unless there are any objections, we should replace the ambiguous descriptions of _overlaps_ with _overlapping areas_ and _overlapping bodies_ (whichever is appropriate on a per method basis).\n\n> But the timing in the descriptions seems inconsistent, which may need to be unified.\n\nI agree, but I'm still fairly unfamiliar with how Godot works under the hood so I haven't been able to identify which timing is correct.\n\nMy assumption would be \"before the physics step\", before everything starts moving again, but I would want confirmation before going ahead with any changes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068838742/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068908679","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108585#issuecomment-3068908679","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108585","id":3068908679,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6269SH","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T10:41:34Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T10:41:34Z","body":"> > but because the descriptions were added in different PRs, they are referred to using different words. Of course, it may also be because of the method name.\n> \n> I think, unless there are any objections, we should replace the ambiguous descriptions of _overlaps_ with _overlapping areas_ and _overlapping bodies_ (whichever is appropriate on a per method basis).\n\nAlthough I think knowing the related methods (of similar names) in the same class gives you the context implied by the class scope.\nHere, just linking `get_overlapping_areas`/`get_overlapping_bodies` in the description to explain these lists for more clarity.\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068908679/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068970979","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108585#issuecomment-3068970979","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108585","id":3068970979,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc627Mfj","user":{"login":"charjr","id":102669158,"node_id":"U_kgDOBh6bZg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102669158?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr","html_url":"https://github.com/charjr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T10:54:34Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T10:55:10Z","body":"> Although I think knowing the related methods (of similar names) in the same class gives you the context implied by the class scope. Here, just linking `get_overlapping_areas`/`get_overlapping_bodies` in the description to explain these lists for more clarity.\n\nAh, are you thinking more along the lines of something like this?\n\n`has_overlapping_bodies`\n> Returns `true` if `get_overlapping_bodies` would return a non-empty list, returns `false` otherwise.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068970979/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3069028877","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108585#issuecomment-3069028877","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108585","id":3069028877,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc627aoN","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T11:07:25Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T11:07:25Z","body":"\nJust explain the list:\n\n```diff\n- For performance reasons (collisions are all processed at the same time) the list of overlapping areas is modified once during the physics step, not immediately after objects are moved. Consider using signals instead.\n+ For performance reasons (collisions are all processed at the same time) the list of overlapping areas (see get_overlapping_areas()) is modified once during the physics step, not immediately after objects are moved. Consider using signals instead.\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3069028877/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]